module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorByBaseModuleLinearIso
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.AffineChartBaseChangePresieve

/-!
# Gluing a comparison into `𝓕 ⊗_R M` over the affine charts of an algebraic space

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B`, let `𝓕` be an
`𝒪_X`-module on the small étale site, let `R` be a commutative ring and let `α : R → 𝒪_X(U₀)` be
a ring homomorphism into the sections over a *terminal* étale chart.
`Stacks.TensorByBaseModule.tensorByBaseModule` then produces the `𝒪_X`-module `𝓕 ⊗_R M` for
every `R`-module `M`, and
`Stacks.TensorByBaseModule.tensorByBaseModuleIsoOfBijectiveApp` identifies it with any
`𝒪_X`-module receiving a comparison from the presheaf `U ↦ 𝓕(U) ⊗_R M` that is bijective on the
sections over the objects of a family whose arrows generate covering sieves.

**On the small étale site of an algebraic space that family is the affine charts.**  This file
records that, and the resulting gluing statement: a comparison bijective on the sections over
every affine chart exhibits its target as `𝓕 ⊗_R M`.  It is the last step of the second part of
[Stacks Project, Tag 073K], where the target is the direct image `g'_*ℱ'` along the base change
of a flat morphism of affine bases: that identification is checked over the affine charts of `X`
— where both sides are computed by Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) — and glued here.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.generate_isAffine_chart_mem`: **the affine charts over an étale chart
  generate a covering sieve**, in the shape the gluing step consumes.  This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.generate_affineChartPresieve_mem` with the presieve
  written out.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.tensorByBaseModuleIsoOfBijectiveOnAffineCharts`: **gluing over the
  affine charts.**

## Implementation notes

*The two spellings of the sheaf of rings agree on the nose.*
`Stacks.TensorByBaseModule.ringSheaf` of the structure sheaf of the small étale ringed site is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtaleRingSheaf` by `rfl` — the first is `Sheaf.mk` of
`ringPresheaf 𝒪_X` and the second the image of `𝒪_X` under `sheafCompose` for the same
forgetful functor, so the two differ only in the sheaf-condition proof — so the `𝒪_X`-modules
of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Modules` are exactly the sheaves of modules the tensor functor
produces, and no transport is needed.  The three site hypotheses that
`Stacks.TensorByBaseModule.tensorByBaseModule` carries —
`GrothendieckTopology.HasSheafCompose` for the forgetful functor to `RingCat`,
`GrothendieckTopology.WEqualsLocallyBijective` and `HasWeakSheafify` for abelian groups — are
all found by instance search for the small étale topology.

*Terminality of the chart is a datum of the construction, not a hypothesis added here.*
`Stacks.TensorByBaseModule.tensorByBaseModule` takes `IsTerminal U₀` as an argument: it is what
makes the constant presheaf of modules a left adjoint and what gives the coefficient map a
source.  An algebraic space has a terminal étale chart exactly when it is representable;
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isTerminal_isAffine_chart` produces one for an affine algebraic
space and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isTerminalIdEtaleChart` for a represented one.

No declaration here carries a `stacks` tag.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 073K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/073K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03ED](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03ED)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite Limits
open Stacks.TensorByBaseModule

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)

/-- The sieve generated by the affine charts over an étale chart is a covering sieve, in the
shape the gluing step of `Stacks.TensorByBaseModule` consumes. -/
theorem generate_isAffine_chart_mem (V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) :
    Sieve.generate (fun {W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (_ : W ⟶ V) =>
        IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W))
      ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1 V :=
  SmallEtale.generate_affineChartPresieve_mem B S hS X.1 V

variable {U₀ : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (hU₀ : IsTerminal U₀) (R : Type u) [CommRing R]
  (𝓕 : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
  (α : R →+* (structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2).val.obj (op U₀))

/-- **Gluing over the affine charts.**  On the small étale site of an algebraic space carrying a
terminal chart, a comparison out of the presheaf `U ↦ 𝓕(U) ⊗_R M` which is bijective on the
sections over every *affine* chart exhibits its target as `𝓕 ⊗_R M`. -/
noncomputable def tensorByBaseModuleIsoOfBijectiveOnAffineCharts (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    (G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (Φ : (tensorByBaseModulePresheaf R hU₀ (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1)
          (structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) 𝓕 α).obj M ⟶
      (PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars (𝟙 (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2).obj)).obj
        ((SheafOfModules.forget (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)).obj G))
    (hbij : ∀ W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1,
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W) →
        Function.Bijective (Φ.app (op W)).hom) :
    (tensorByBaseModule R hU₀ (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1)
        (structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) 𝓕 α).obj M ≅ G :=
  tensorByBaseModuleIsoOfBijectiveApp R hU₀ (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1)
    (structureSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2) 𝓕 α M G Φ
    (fun W => IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W))
    (generate_isAffine_chart_mem B S hS X) hbij

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
